---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Contact and Corrections"
  description="How to contact Betting Maths about calculation errors, factual corrections, broken pages and site issues."
>
  <section class="content-card">
    <p class="eyebrow">Contact and corrections</p>
    <h1>Contact Betting Maths</h1>
    <p class="lead">If you find a calculation error, factual problem or broken page, we want to know about it.</p>
    <div class="callout"><strong>Best route for corrections:</strong> report a reproducible issue through the public Betting Maths GitHub issue tracker. Please include the page, the inputs used and the result you expected where possible.</div>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/Camackazi/betting-maths/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer">Report an Issue on GitHub</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/editorial-standards/">Read Editorial Standards</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>What to include in a calculation report</h2>
    <ul class="standard-list">
      <li>The URL of the calculator or guide.</li>
      <li>The inputs you entered.</li>
      <li>The result Betting Maths displayed.</li>
      <li>The result you expected and how you calculated it.</li>
      <li>Any bookmaker, exchange or settlement rule that materially affects the example.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>A reproducible example helps separate a calculation bug from a difference in assumptions or settlement rules.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Corrections policy</h2>
    <p>If a formula, worked example or factual statement is wrong, our priority is to correct it. Material issues should be reflected in the page rather than hidden behind vague wording.</p>
    <p>Our <a href="/methodology/">calculation methodology</a> explains the standard formulas and assumptions used across the site.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>What we cannot help with</h2>
    <table class="contact-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Best next step</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>A bookmaker account or withdrawal</td><td>Contact the bookmaker directly.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>A disputed or settled bet</td><td>Check the operator's settlement rules and customer-support process.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Personal betting advice or tips</td><td>Betting Maths does not provide selections or personal betting advice.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>A site calculation or factual error</td><td>Use the Betting Maths GitHub issue tracker.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Responsible gambling support</h2>
    <p>If betting is causing stress, financial difficulty or loss of control, use the dedicated responsible gambling page for current support resources rather than the technical issue tracker.</p>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="/responsible-gambling/">Responsible Gambling Support</a></div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .article-section { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
    .standard-list { padding-left: 1.3rem; }
    .standard-list li { margin: 0.45rem 0; }
    .article-section a { color: var(--color-green-dark); font-weight: 800; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
    .contact-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: white; margin: 1rem 0; }
    .contact-table th, .contact-table td { padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
    .contact-table th { color: var(--color-navy); background: #f4f7fa; }
  </style>
</MainLayout>
